IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part4`

-- Tests for wa-interpretation-part4.l4 (ss 28 to 32).  Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Tests -- Part IV`

-- s 28: an Act passed after 13 April 1853 is a public Act unless the contrary is expressly provided.
#ASSERT `an Act is deemed a public Act and judicially noticed as such` (Date 14 4 1853) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act is deemed a public Act and judicially noticed as such` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act is deemed a public Act and judicially noticed as such` (Date 13 4 1853) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act is deemed a public Act and judicially noticed as such` (Date 1 1 1800) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act is deemed a public Act and judicially noticed as such` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 29, s 30: one answer each, with or without the feature the section is about
#ASSERT `a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment` TRUE
#ASSERT `a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment` FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act may be amended or repealed` TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act may be amended or repealed` FALSE
-- s 31
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 31` `a preamble` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 31` `an appendix` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 31` `a schedule` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 31` `a table` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 31` `notes to an appendix, schedule or table` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a marginal note is not dealt with by s 31
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 31` `a marginal note` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a preamble is construed as intended to assist in explaining the written law's purport and object`
-- s 32
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 32` `a Part heading` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 32` `a division heading` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 32` `a subdivision heading` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 32` `a marginal note` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 32` `a footnote` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 32` `a heading to a section, regulation, rule, local law, bylaw or clause, or to a portion of one` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- fork F8: where there is a marginal note the text does not say
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 32` `a heading to a section, regulation, rule, local law, bylaw or clause, or to a portion of one` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an appendix is dealt with by s 31, not by s 32
#ASSERT `forms part of the written law under section 32` `a schedule` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
